@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-88-definitions`

-- Tests for s 88 (definitions of Part 5). Every expected value was worked by hand from the definitions
-- (the arithmetic is written beside each group) before the assertion was run. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- All holdings, prices and index readings are HYPOTHETICAL scenario values, not published figures.

§ `Tests of section 88`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- A holding in the right to profits only.
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
`a profits holding of` f MEANS
    `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons` WITH
        `fraction of the right to profits`                                              IS f
        `fraction of the right to appoint a director or general manager`                IS 0
        `fraction of the voting rights in the general meeting`                          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to a share of the surplus assets on winding up`          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to direct the holder of a right in (1) to (4) on how to use it` IS 0

-- A holding in the voting rights only.
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
`a voting holding of` f MEANS
    `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons` WITH
        `fraction of the right to profits`                                              IS 0
        `fraction of the right to appoint a director or general manager`                IS 0
        `fraction of the voting rights in the general meeting`                          IS f
        `fraction of the right to a share of the surplus assets on winding up`          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to direct the holder of a right in (1) to (4) on how to use it` IS 0

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person who may hold together with the person`
`a sibling's profits holding of` f MEANS
    `A person who may hold together with the person` WITH
        `holdings` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `tie to the person` IS `a tie of paragraph (1)` `sibling`
        `regularly cooperates with the person by agreement on material matters of the body` IS FALSE

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person who may hold together with the person`
`a sibling's voting holding of` f MEANS
    `A person who may hold together with the person` WITH
        `holdings` IS `a voting holding of` f
        `tie to the person` IS `a tie of paragraph (1)` `sibling`
        `regularly cooperates with the person by agreement on material matters of the body` IS FALSE

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person who may hold together with the person`
`a cooperating stranger's profits holding of` f MEANS
    `A person who may hold together with the person` WITH
        `holdings` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `tie to the person` IS `no tie`
        `regularly cooperates with the person by agreement on material matters of the body` IS TRUE

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person who may hold together with the person`
`a stranger's profits holding of` f MEANS
    `A person who may hold together with the person` WITH
        `holdings` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `tie to the person` IS `no tie`
        `regularly cooperates with the person by agreement on material matters of the body` IS FALSE

GIVETH A LIST OF `A person who may hold together with the person`
`no others` MEANS EMPTY

§§ `"Relative" (source lines 3296-3301)`
-- Paragraph (1) and (2) ties are relatives; (3): (25%) or more of one kind; (4): a trustee.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a tie of paragraph (1)` `spouse`)
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a tie of paragraph (1)` `parent of a parent`)
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a tie of paragraph (1)` `the spouse of a spouse, sibling, parent, parent of a parent, descendant, or descendant of a spouse`)
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a tie of paragraph (2)` `sibling of a parent`)
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a tie of paragraph (2)` `descendant of a sibling`)
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a body of persons held by the person or by a relative of the person` (25%))
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a body of persons held by the person or by a relative of the person` (24.99%))
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a person who holds the person` (60%))
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a body of persons held by one who holds the person` (25%))
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a body of persons held by one who holds the person` (10%))
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` `a trustee as paragraph (4) describes`
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` `no tie`
-- For the exemption in s 97 only paragraphs (1) and (2) count (source line 3301).
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` (`a tie of paragraph (1)` `sibling`)
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` (`a tie of paragraph (2)` `descendant of a sibling`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` (`a body of persons held by the person or by a relative of the person` (90%))
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` `a trustee as paragraph (4) describes`
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` `no tie`

§§ `"Material shareholder": (10%) of any one kind, alone or together with another (source lines 3256-3257)`
-- Alone: (10%) is enough, (9.99%) is not (the definition: "(10%) at least").
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (10%)) `with the others` `no others` `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (9.99%)) `with the others` `no others` `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
-- (6%) + a sibling's (4%) = (10%): material, under one other and under many.
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (6%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
-- (6%) + (3.99%) = (9.99%): not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (6%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (3.99%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
-- (4%) + two siblings of (4%) each: (12%) with both, at most (8%) with one. Fork S1.
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%), `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `together with any number of others, their holdings added`
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%), `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `together with one other person only`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%), `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` BECAUSE "section 88 says \"together with another\", and here one other person and several others give different answers"
-- A cooperating non-relative counts; a stranger does not.
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a cooperating stranger's profits holding of` (6%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a stranger's profits holding of` (6%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
-- The kinds are not added across: (9%) of the profits and a sibling's (9%) of the votes is no kind at (10%).
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a profits holding of` (9%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's voting holding of` (9%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
-- (9%) of the profits, then (10%) of the votes held by the person: "at least (10%) in one or more of any kind" is met by the votes.
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder` (`a voting holding of` (10%)) `with the others` `no others` `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer`

§§ `A material shareholder at the time of sale or in the twelve months before it (fork S4)`
-- Sale on 15 March 2026. The twelve months before: from 15 March 2025 (first reading) or 16 March 2025 (second).
-- A record on 14 March 2025 is outside both. A record on 15 March 2025 is inside the first reading only.
-- A record on 16 March 2025 is inside both. A record on the sale day itself is inside. A record after it is ignored.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The holdings of a person on one day`
`a profits record on` d `of` f MEANS
    `The holdings of a person on one day` WITH
        `the day` IS d
        `the person's own holdings that day` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `the others who may hold together with the person that day` IS `no others`

`the readings taken by default` MEANS
    `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C` WITH
        `together with another`                   IS `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
        `counting the days of a period`           IS `declined where the way of counting changes the answer`
        `half the holding expenses`               IS `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer`
        `the twelve months before a day`          IS `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`
        `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `a cap where the gain stands in several bands` IS `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer`
        `where each part stands in the top layer` IS `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 125B(3)` IS `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)` IS `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer`
        `the real gain for the middle part` IS `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`
        `the naming of a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the twelve months before a day`
GIVETH AN `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the readings with the twelve months read as` r MEANS
    `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C` WITH
        `together with another`                   IS `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
        `counting the days of a period`           IS `declined where the way of counting changes the answer`
        `half the holding expenses`               IS `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer`
        `the twelve months before a day`          IS r
        `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `a cap where the gain stands in several bands` IS `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer`
        `where each part stands in the top layer` IS `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 125B(3)` IS `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)` IS `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer`
        `the real gain for the middle part` IS `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`
        `the naming of a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

`the sale day for the twelve months` MEANS YMD 2026 3 15

-- 14 March 2025: outside the twelve months on every reading: not material, the readings agree, so the default answers FALSE.
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 14) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default`
-- 15 March 2025: inside the first reading, outside the second: the default declines.
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 15) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` (`the readings with the twelve months read as` `the twelve months begin on the day twelve months before`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 15) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` (`the readings with the twelve months read as` `the twelve months begin on the day after the day twelve months before`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 15) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default` BECAUSE "section 88 does not say from which day the twelve months before a day run, and here the first day changes the answer"
-- 16 March 2025: inside both: the default answers TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 16) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default`
-- The sale day itself: inside.
#ASSERT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default`
-- The day after the sale: ignored.
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 3 16) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default`
-- A record of (9.99%) is not material on any day.
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `of` (9.99%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default`
-- No record at all: not material, as far as the rule can tell.
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (EMPTY) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default`

§§ `"Asset" (source lines 3258-3262)`
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What is sold`
`the thing sold, personal movables` a `inventory` b `possessory right` c `betterment right` d MEANS
    `What is sold` WITH
        `movables of an individual held for the personal use of the individual, family or dependants` IS a
        `business inventory` IS b
        `a possessory right in land used for living and not for gain` IS c
        `a right in land or in a land association on whose sale betterment tax is imposed, or would be but for an exemption` IS d
#ASSERT `s 88 — the thing is an asset` (`the thing sold, personal movables` FALSE `inventory` FALSE `possessory right` FALSE `betterment right` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the thing is an asset` (`the thing sold, personal movables` TRUE `inventory` FALSE `possessory right` FALSE `betterment right` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the thing is an asset` (`the thing sold, personal movables` FALSE `inventory` TRUE `possessory right` FALSE `betterment right` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the thing is an asset` (`the thing sold, personal movables` FALSE `inventory` FALSE `possessory right` TRUE `betterment right` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the thing is an asset` (`the thing sold, personal movables` FALSE `inventory` FALSE `possessory right` FALSE `betterment right` TRUE)

§§ `"Original price" (source lines 3269-3281)`
-- Each way of acquisition gives the amount the way names; the closing words add the expenses not deducted before.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`bought` 500_000) EQUALS 500_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`received in exchange` 450_000) EQUALS 450_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`received as a gift before 3 December 1951` 10_000) EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`received as a gift from 3 December 1951 to 31 March 1968` 20_000) EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`received as a gift from 1 April 1968, not from a relative` 1_100_000) EQUALS 1_100_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`received as a gift from 1 April 1968 that is exempt under section 97(a)(4) or (5)` 300_000) EQUALS 300_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`received as a gift from 1 April 1968 from a relative, not exempt` 1_100_000) EQUALS 1_100_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`inherited` 700_000) EQUALS 700_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`created by the taxpayer` 90_000) EQUALS 90_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price, before the additions of the closing words,` (`arrived in some other way` 80_000) EQUALS 80_000
-- 500,000 + 35,000 of improvement and holding expenses not deducted before = 535,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the original price` (`bought` 500_000) `with the improvement and holding expenses not deducted before` 35_000 EQUALS 535_000

§§ `"Purchase day" (source lines 3283-3285)`
GIVEN reached  IS A DATE
      entitled IS A DATE
      gift     IS A BOOLEAN
      lastday  IS A MAYBE DATE
      heir     IS A BOOLEAN
      decday   IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The facts that settle the purchase day`
`the purchase facts:` reached `, entitled` entitled `, gift` gift `, last acquirer's day` lastday `, inherited` heir `, decedent's day` decday MEANS
    `The facts that settle the purchase day` WITH
        `the day the asset reached the taxpayer` IS reached
        `the day the taxpayer became entitled to it` IS entitled
        `a gift before 1 April 1968, or a gift exempt under section 97(a)(4) or (5) at any time` IS gift
        `the day the asset reached the last acquirer other than by an exempt gift` IS lastday
        `inherited from one who died after 31 March 1981, or by waiver of inheritance` IS heir
        `the day that would have been the purchase day had the decedent sold` IS decday
-- The earlier of reaching and entitlement: reached 1 June 2010, entitled 1 March 2010 -> 1 March 2010; and the reverse.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the purchase day` (`the purchase facts:` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, entitled` (YMD 2010 3 1) `, gift` FALSE `, last acquirer's day` NOTHING `, inherited` FALSE `, decedent's day` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2010 3 1
#ASSERT `s 88 — the purchase day` (`the purchase facts:` (YMD 2010 3 1) `, entitled` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, gift` FALSE `, last acquirer's day` NOTHING `, inherited` FALSE `, decedent's day` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2010 3 1
-- A gift of the old kind: the day the last non-exempt acquirer received it, 1 July 1960, not the day of the gift, 1 June 2010.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the purchase day` (`the purchase facts:` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, entitled` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, gift` TRUE `, last acquirer's day` (JUST (YMD 1960 7 1)) `, inherited` FALSE `, decedent's day` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 1960 7 1
-- An inheritance from one who died after 31 March 1981: the day that would have been the decedent's purchase day.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the purchase day` (`the purchase facts:` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, entitled` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, gift` FALSE `, last acquirer's day` NOTHING `, inherited` TRUE `, decedent's day` (JUST (YMD 1999 2 3))) EQUALS YMD 1999 2 3
-- The gift case with the last acquirer's day not supplied is declined by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — the purchase day` (`the purchase facts:` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, entitled` (YMD 2010 6 1) `, gift` TRUE `, last acquirer's day` NOTHING `, inherited` FALSE `, decedent's day` NOTHING) BECAUSE "the day s 88 names as the purchase day was not supplied"

§§ `"Consideration" (source line 3295)`
GIVEN market IS A NUMBER
      agreed IS A NUMBER
      good   IS A BOOLEAN
      land   IS A BOOLEAN
      writ   IS A BOOLEAN
      exp    IS A NUMBER
      redeem IS A BOOLEAN
      diff   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The facts that settle the consideration`
`the price facts:` market `, agreed` agreed `, officer satisfied` good `, land` land `, in writing` writ `, expenses` exp `, redemption` redeem `, index differences` diff MEANS
    `The facts that settle the consideration` WITH
        `the price to be expected from a willing seller to a willing buyer, the asset free of any charge securing a debt` IS market
        `the price agreed` IS agreed
        `the assessing officer is satisfied the agreed price was fixed in good faith, uninfluenced by special relations between seller and buyer` IS good
        `a right in land` IS land
        `the sale was made in writing` IS writ
        `the expenses of the sale the taxpayer incurred in that sale` IS exp
        `a bond or commercial security is redeemed` IS redeem
        `the index differences on the redemption` IS diff
-- The agreed price counts: 1,000,000 less expenses 20,000 = 980,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the consideration` (`the price facts:` 1_200_000 `, agreed` 1_000_000 `, officer satisfied` TRUE `, land` FALSE `, in writing` FALSE `, expenses` 20_000 `, redemption` FALSE `, index differences` 0) EQUALS 980_000
-- Land, officer satisfied, but not in writing: the market price, 1,200,000, less 20,000 = 1,180,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the consideration` (`the price facts:` 1_200_000 `, agreed` 1_000_000 `, officer satisfied` TRUE `, land` TRUE `, in writing` FALSE `, expenses` 20_000 `, redemption` FALSE `, index differences` 0) EQUALS 1_180_000
-- Land, in writing, officer satisfied: the agreed price, 1,000,000 less 20,000 = 980,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the consideration` (`the price facts:` 1_200_000 `, agreed` 1_000_000 `, officer satisfied` TRUE `, land` TRUE `, in writing` TRUE `, expenses` 20_000 `, redemption` FALSE `, index differences` 0) EQUALS 980_000
-- The officer is not satisfied: the market price, 1,200,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the consideration` (`the price facts:` 1_200_000 `, agreed` 1_000_000 `, officer satisfied` FALSE `, land` FALSE `, in writing` FALSE `, expenses` 0 `, redemption` FALSE `, index differences` 0) EQUALS 1_200_000
-- The redemption of a bond: the index differences, 5,000, are part of the consideration: 100,000 + 5,000 = 105,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the consideration` (`the price facts:` 100_000 `, agreed` 100_000 `, officer satisfied` TRUE `, land` FALSE `, in writing` FALSE `, expenses` 0 `, redemption` TRUE `, index differences` 5_000) EQUALS 105_000

§§ `Capital gain, capital loss, adjusted price, inflationary amount, real capital gain (source lines 3289, 3302-3304, 3310, 3316)`
GIVEN cons IS A NUMBER
      rem  IS A NUMBER
      imps IS A LIST OF `An improvement of the asset`
      hold IS A NUMBER
      isale IS A NUMBER
      ibuy  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale of an asset`
`the sale:` cons `, remaining price` rem `, improvements` imps `, holding expenses` hold `, index at sale` isale `, index at purchase` ibuy MEANS
    `A sale of an asset` WITH
        `consideration`                      IS cons
        `remaining original price`           IS rem
        `improvements`                       IS imps
        `remaining holding expenses`         IS hold
        `index on the sale day`              IS isale
        `index on the purchase day`          IS ibuy
        `index on 31 December 1993`          IS 100
        `purchase day`                       IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `sale day`                           IS YMD 2020 1 1

GIVEN e IS A NUMBER
      i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An improvement of the asset`
`an improvement with remaining expense` e `finished at index` i MEANS
    `An improvement of the asset` WITH
        `remaining expense of the improvement` IS e
        `index on the day the improvement was finished` IS i

`the lost reading` MEANS `the half of the holding expenses that is left out is lost from the adjusted price`
`the added-back reading` MEANS `the half of the holding expenses that is left out is added back, not indexed`

-- Plain: consideration 1,200,000, remaining price 800,000, indices 120 over 100, nothing else.
--   capital gain = 1,200,000 - 800,000 = 400,000
--   adjusted price = 800,000 x 120/100 = 960,000 ; excess over the remaining price = 160,000
--   inflationary amount = the part of the gain equal to 160,000 = 160,000
--   real capital gain = 400,000 - 160,000 = 240,000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital gain` (`the sale:` 1_200_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 400_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital loss` (`the sale:` 1_200_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 88 — the adjusted remaining original price of` 800_000 `with the improvements` (EMPTY) `and the holding expenses` 0 `at the index` 120 `over` 100 `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 960_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the inflationary amount of` (`the sale:` 1_200_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 160_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain of` (`the sale:` 1_200_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 240_000
-- With no holding expenses the readings of fork S3 agree, so the default answers too.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain of` (`the sale:` 1_200_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer` EQUALS 240_000
-- The inflationary amount cannot exceed the gain: consideration 900,000: gain 100,000, excess 160,000, inflationary amount 100,000, real gain 0.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the inflationary amount of` (`the sale:` 900_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 100_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain of` (`the sale:` 900_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 0
-- A loss: consideration 700,000 against 800,000: no gain, a loss of 100,000, no inflationary amount, no real gain.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital gain` (`the sale:` 700_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital loss` (`the sale:` 700_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 100_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the inflationary amount of` (`the sale:` 700_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 0
-- Consideration equal to the remaining price: neither gain nor loss.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital gain` (`the sale:` 800_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital loss` (`the sale:` 800_000 `, remaining price` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 120 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 0

-- With an improvement and holding expenses: remaining price 1,000,000 of which an improvement of 200,000 finished at index 110
-- and holding expenses of 100,000; consideration 1,500,000; index at sale 132, at purchase 100.
--   capital gain = 1,500,000 - 1,000,000 = 500,000
--   part indexed from purchase = (1,000,000 - 200,000 - 100,000/2) x 132/100 = 750,000 x 1.32 = 990,000
--   the improvement indexed from its own day = 200,000 x 132/110 = 240,000
--   adjusted price, the half lost: 990,000 + 240,000 = 1,230,000 ; excess over 1,000,000 = 230,000
--   adjusted price, the half added back: 1,230,000 + 50,000 = 1,280,000 ; excess = 280,000
--   inflationary amount: 230,000 or 280,000, both below the gain 500,000
--   real capital gain: 270,000 or 220,000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the adjusted remaining original price of` 1_000_000 `with the improvements` (LIST `an improvement with remaining expense` 200_000 `finished at index` 110) `and the holding expenses` 100_000 `at the index` 132 `over` 100 `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 1_230_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the adjusted remaining original price of` 1_000_000 `with the improvements` (LIST `an improvement with remaining expense` 200_000 `finished at index` 110) `and the holding expenses` 100_000 `at the index` 132 `over` 100 `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the added-back reading` EQUALS 1_280_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — the adjusted remaining original price of` 1_000_000 `with the improvements` (LIST `an improvement with remaining expense` 200_000 `finished at index` 110) `and the holding expenses` 100_000 `at the index` 132 `over` 100 `, reading half the holding expenses as` `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer` BECAUSE "section 88 leaves open what becomes of the half of the holding expenses that the adjusted price leaves out, and here it changes the answer"
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain of` (`the sale:` 1_500_000 `, remaining price` 1_000_000 `, improvements` (LIST `an improvement with remaining expense` 200_000 `finished at index` 110) `, holding expenses` 100_000 `, index at sale` 132 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 270_000
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain of` (`the sale:` 1_500_000 `, remaining price` 1_000_000 `, improvements` (LIST `an improvement with remaining expense` 200_000 `finished at index` 110) `, holding expenses` 100_000 `, index at sale` 132 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the added-back reading` EQUALS 220_000
-- Improvements and no holding expenses: the readings agree. (1,000,000 - 200,000) x 1.32 + 240,000 = 1,056,000 + 240,000 = 1,296,000 ;
-- excess 296,000 ; real gain 500,000 - 296,000 = 204,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain of` (`the sale:` 1_500_000 `, remaining price` 1_000_000 `, improvements` (LIST `an improvement with remaining expense` 200_000 `finished at index` 110) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 132 `, index at purchase` 100) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer` EQUALS 204_000

§§ `"Chargeable inflationary amount" (source lines 3307-3309)`
GIVEN rem  IS A NUMBER
      imps IS A LIST OF `An improvement of the asset`
      hold IS A NUMBER
      i93  IS A NUMBER
      ibuy IS A NUMBER
      d    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The asset on 31 December 1993`
`the asset in 1993:` rem `, improvements` imps `, holding expenses` hold `, index 1993` i93 `, index at purchase` ibuy `, bought` d MEANS
    `The asset on 31 December 1993` WITH
        `remaining original price on 31 December 1993` IS rem
        `improvements finished by 31 December 1993` IS imps
        `remaining holding expenses on 31 December 1993` IS hold
        `index on 31 December 1993` IS i93
        `index on the purchase day` IS ibuy
        `purchase day` IS d
-- 800,000 x 110/100 = 880,000 ; less 800,000 = 80,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the chargeable inflationary amount of` (`the asset in 1993:` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index 1993` 110 `, index at purchase` 100 `, bought` (YMD 1990 5 1)) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 80_000
-- With an improvement of 100,000 finished at index 110 (the 1993 index): (800,000 - 100,000) x 1.10 + 100,000 x 110/110 = 770,000 + 100,000 = 870,000 ; less 800,000 = 70,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the chargeable inflationary amount of` (`the asset in 1993:` 800_000 `, improvements` (LIST `an improvement with remaining expense` 100_000 `finished at index` 110) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index 1993` 110 `, index at purchase` 100 `, bought` (YMD 1990 5 1)) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 70_000
-- Bought on 31 December 1993: the sale on that day is possible, one-day-old index: excess 0 here (index 100 over 100) -> 0.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the chargeable inflationary amount of` (`the asset in 1993:` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index 1993` 100 `, index at purchase` 100 `, bought` (YMD 1993 12 31)) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 0
-- Bought on 1 January 1994 or later: nothing could have been sold on 31 December 1993; the amount is nought (assumption A5).
#ASSERT `s 88 — the chargeable inflationary amount of` (`the asset in 1993:` 800_000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index 1993` 110 `, index at purchase` 100 `, bought` (YMD 1994 1 1)) `, reading half the holding expenses as` `the lost reading` EQUALS 0

§§ `The real capital gain up to the fixed date, from it to the change date, and the rest (source lines 3311-3314)`
-- Fork S2. The fixed date is 1 January 2003, the change date 1 January 2012 (source lines 3267, 3312).
#ASSERT `s 88 — the fixed date` EQUALS YMD 2003 1 1
#ASSERT `s 88 — the change date` EQUALS YMD 2012 1 1
-- Counting the days "from A to B":
--   2002-01-01 to 2002-12-31: 364 days between, 365 counting both ends.
#ASSERT `the days from` (YMD 2002 1 1) `to` (YMD 2002 12 31) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 364
#ASSERT `the days from` (YMD 2002 1 1) `to` (YMD 2002 12 31) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 365
#ASSERT REFUSED `the days from` (YMD 2002 1 1) `to` (YMD 2002 12 31) `, reading the count as` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` BECAUSE "section 88 does not say how the days of a period are counted, and here the way of counting changes the answer"
-- An empty period (the end before the start) is nought on both countings: 2003-01-01 to 2002-12-31.
#ASSERT `the days from` (YMD 2003 1 1) `to` (YMD 2002 12 31) `, reading the count as` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` EQUALS 0
-- Up to the fixed date. Bought 2002-01-01, sold 2004-09-27 (1,000 days later: 365 + 365 + 270): real gain 1,001,000.
--   between: 1,001,000 x 364/1,000 = 364,364.   both ends: 1,001,000 x 365/1,001 = 365,000.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 1_001_000 `bought on` (YMD 2002 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2004 9 27) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 364_364
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 1_001_000 `bought on` (YMD 2002 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2004 9 27) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 365_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 1_001_000 `bought on` (YMD 2002 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2004 9 27) `, reading the count as` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` BECAUSE "section 88 does not say how the days of a period are counted, and here the way of counting changes the answer"
-- Bought on or after the fixed date: nothing accrued up to it, on every counting (2003-01-01 bought, sold 2020-12-29).
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 43_197_756 `bought on` (YMD 2003 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 12 29) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 43_197_756 `bought on` (YMD 2003 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 12 29) `, reading the count as` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` EQUALS 0
-- A sale before the fixed date is outside the definition.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 1_000 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2002 12 31) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` BECAUSE "section 88 defines the real capital gain up to the fixed date for a sale on or after the fixed date"

-- Bought 2003-01-01, sold 2020-12-29 (6,572 days later); real gain 43,197,756 = 6,572 x 6,573.
--   N2: 2003-01-01 to 2011-12-31 = 3,286 days between, 3,287 both ends. D: 6,572 between, 6,573 both ends.
--   between: after the fixed date up to the change date = 43,197,756 x 3,286/6,572 = 21,598,878 ; the rest = 43,197,756 - 21,598,878 = 21,598,878.
--   both ends: 43,197,756 x 3,287/6,573 = 6,572 x 3,287 = 21,602,164 ; the rest = 43,197,756 - 21,602,164 = 21,595,592.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` 43_197_756 `bought on` (YMD 2003 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 12 29) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 21_598_878
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` 43_197_756 `bought on` (YMD 2003 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 12 29) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 21_602_164
#ASSERT `s 88 — the remainder of the real capital gain after the change date, of` 43_197_756 `bought on` (YMD 2003 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 12 29) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 21_598_878
#ASSERT `s 88 — the remainder of the real capital gain after the change date, of` 43_197_756 `bought on` (YMD 2003 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 12 29) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 21_595_592
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` 43_197_756 `bought on` (YMD 2003 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 12 29) `, reading the count as` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` BECAUSE "section 88 does not say how the days of a period are counted, and here the way of counting changes the answer"
-- Bought 2000-01-01, sold 2020-01-01 (7,305 days; 7,306 both ends); real gain 53,370,330 = 7,305 x 7,306.
--   N1: 1,095 between / 1,096 both ends. N2: 3,286 / 3,287.
--   between: up to the fixed date = 7,306 x 1,095 = 8,000,070 ; to the change date = 7,306 x 3,286 = 24,007,516 ;
--            the rest = 53,370,330 - 8,000,070 - 24,007,516 = 21,362,744.
--   both ends: 7,305 x 1,096 = 8,006,280 ; 7,305 x 3,287 = 24,011,535 ; the rest = 53,370,330 - 8,006,280 - 24,011,535 = 21,352,515.
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 53_370_330 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 8_000_070
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` 53_370_330 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 24_007_516
#ASSERT `s 88 — the remainder of the real capital gain after the change date, of` 53_370_330 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, reading the count as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 21_362_744
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` 53_370_330 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 8_006_280
#ASSERT `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` 53_370_330 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 24_011_535
#ASSERT `s 88 — the remainder of the real capital gain after the change date, of` 53_370_330 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 21_352_515
-- A sale before the change date is outside the two later parts.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` 1_000 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2011 12 31) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` BECAUSE "section 88 defines the parts of the real capital gain around the change date for a sale on or after the change date"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 88 — the remainder of the real capital gain after the change date, of` 1_000 `bought on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `and sold on` (YMD 2011 12 31) `, reading the count as` `both the first and the last day are counted` BECAUSE "section 88 defines the parts of the real capital gain around the change date for a sale on or after the change date"

§§ `The status as a MAYBE: NOTHING where the readings part, JUST the answer where they agree`
-- 14 March 2025: outside every reading: JUST FALSE. 15 March 2025: the first reading true, the second false: NOTHING.
-- 16 March 2025: inside every reading: JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 14) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 15) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 16) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` `the readings taken by default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder on` `the sale day for the twelve months` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 3 15) `of` (10%)) `, reading the forks as` (`the readings with the twelve months read as` `the twelve months begin on the day twelve months before`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- At one moment: 4% and two siblings of 4%: many says material, one says not: NOTHING by default; each reading by name.
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder, at one moment,` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%), `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder, at one moment,` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%), `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `together with any number of others, their holdings added` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder, at one moment,` (`a profits holding of` (4%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%), `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `together with one other person only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where they agree (6% and one sibling of 4%): JUST TRUE by default.
#ASSERT `s 88 — whether a material shareholder, at one moment,` (`a profits holding of` (6%)) `with the others` (LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` (4%)) `, reading together with another as` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
